      "nets": ["NET0004"],
      "observed": "On the Microcontroller sheet (mcu.kicad_sch, tile 2/4) the WS2812B status LED D9 has its data input DIN (pin 4) wired to global label NET0004, but NET0004 does not appear on any pin of the ESP32-C3 (U9) anywhere in the drawing (the MCU's global labels are NET0001/2/3/7/8/10/11/13/14/17/18 only). VDD (pin 1) is on +3V3 and GND (pin 3) is tied, but the data line is left dangling.",
      "expected": "The specification states the board exposes status over 'a single onboard WS2812B status LED (D1)' and the firmware (led.rs) drives it per state; the DIN line must connect to an ESP32 GPIO.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "mcu.kicad_sch tile 2/4: D9 WS2812B pin4 DIN -> NET0004 (label terminates with no matching MCU pin); MCU tile 1/4 shows no NET0004 label on U9"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "a single onboard WS2812B status LED (D1)"}
      ],
      "impact": "The WS2812B never receives serial data, so the onboard status LED stays off / undefined; the board loses its intended visual status indication (Wi-Fi/run/fault colors).",
      "confidence": 0.6
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Tracing the SPI, heater, power-mux, buck and USB paths matches the specification, but the WS2812B status LED's DIN (NET0004) is not connected to any ESP32 pin in the drawing, leaving the status LED undriven - an open-connection anomaly."
}

